<title>USA: Countrywide added to S&amp;P 500 Index.</title>
<headline>Countrywide added to S&amp;P 500 Index.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's said on Wednesday that its Financial Information Services group will add Countrywide Credit Industries Inc to its S&amp;P 500 Index, replacing USLIFE Corp.</p>
<p>USLIFE is being acquired by American General Corp, which also is a component of the S&amp;P 500 Index, Standard &amp; Poor's said in a news release.</p>
<p>Countrywide, based in Pasadena, Calif., is a mortgage banking business. It will be added to the index's consumer finance industry group in the financial economic sector.</p>
<p>Countrywide shares closed up 1/4 to 27-1/4 in New York Stock Exchange trading.</p>
